    "result": "Fixed! The bug was a floating-point precision issue in the `parseEuros` and `cellCents` functions in `src/money.js`.\n\n**The problem:** When converting \"39.95\" to cents, the calculation `Number * 100` produced `3995.0000000000005` instead of `3995`, which failed the integer validation.\n\n**The solution:** Use `Math.round()` to ensure the result is always a whole number:\n- Changed `Number(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')).toFixed(2)) * 100` \u2192 `Math.round(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')) * 100)`\n- Applied the same fix to `cellCents` for consistency\n\nAll 51 tests pass, including the reproduction case. You can now add your gym membership with `subtrack add Gym 39.95 --since 2026-10-03`.",
